<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for direct distribution (Developer ID +
  notarization).

  DELIBERATELY EMPTY. It carried three relaxations —
    com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit
    com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory
    com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation
  — taken from plans/MACOS_DMG_RUST_REPACKAGING_PLAN.md:202-203 on the
  assumption that ONNX Runtime generates executable code and that PyInstaller's
  dlopen'd libraries would trip library validation. Neither was ever measured,
  because no Developer ID certificate existed when they were written.

  Measured 2026-08-21, once one did. With this file empty and the hardened
  runtime enforced, the bundled interpreter completed a full catalog pass:
  5 files, 117 chunks, 117 chunk_vectors. 117 real ONNX inferences, no JIT
  entitlement. Removing them one at a time and all together made no difference.

  The harness was checked for the failure it was supposed to be able to detect,
  rather than trusted because it went green: `codesign -dvv` showed
  flags=0x10000(runtime) throughout, and DYLD_PRINT_LIBRARIES=1 produced no
  output — the runtime stripping DYLD_* is exactly what it does without
  com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables, so enforcement was
  live and a genuine violation would have been killed.

  PyInstaller is also gone (see plans/EMBEDDED_CPYTHON_SIDECAR.md), which
  retired the library-validation argument independently: every .so in the
  bundle is signed with the same Team ID, which is what validation asks for.

  BEFORE ADDING ONE BACK: reproduce the failure with the entitlement absent and
  record what died. An empty file is worth keeping empty — each relaxation
  widens the attack surface of a process that reads the user's entire library,
  and each is a question at App Store review, where the first two are refused
  outright.

  Verified scope, stated so the next person knows what was not covered:
  startup, markdown and PNG extraction, chunking, embedding, the vector store
  and the scheduler. Not exercised: PDF/EPUB extraction, transcription (not
  bundled), or a provider call over the network. All are ahead-of-time compiled
  and none is a plausible JIT, but they were not run.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
